        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-fabedfca6889",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, travel by boat along the Beni River to Madidi National Park. The boat journey takes about 3–4 hours.\n\nThe route then follows the smaller Tuichi River, where you can watch for birds and mammals. Arrive at Caquihuara Ecolodge inside the park. There are seven walking trails of varying lengths and difficulty.\n\nAt night, take a short walk through the Amazon rainforest. The forest sounds quite different after dark, and many animals become more active.\n\nIncluded: one night at Caquihuara Ecolodge in a shared room with a shared bathroom, boat transfers, guided walks and the services of a local guide. Meals: breakfast, lunch and dinner."
    },
